From: vera-research local fixes <sp2117@oz.gccis.rit.edu>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vera-research: importable one-video inference fixes for
 generate_initial_score.py

- guard the script body in main() so the classes can be imported without side effects
- drop imports the inference path never uses (pandas, decord, pdb, pytorch_lightning, peft)
- VideoAnomalyDetectionModelInference: nn.Module instead of pl.LightningModule (container only)
- forward(): use self.generation_config (was the script global) and keep raw responses
- dataset: raise instead of substituting a random other video on a load error
- main(): take the single label from forward()'s list instead of calling .item() on a list

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
